# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Copied into out/ verbatim by `next export`
# (files under public/ land at the export root), so this ships with every
# deploy without extra build steps.
#
# Why this exists: iOS "Add to Home Screen" apps run in a standalone
# WKWebView with no reload button and no pull-to-refresh, and this app has
# no service worker to bust. Without an explicit Cache-Control, index.html
# (and every other page) fell back to default/heuristic caching, so a fix
# already deployed to production stayed invisible in the home-screen app
# until the icon was deleted and re-added. The pages themselves are cheap to
# refetch — the actual weight is in /_next/static, which is content-hashed
# and safe to cache forever.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
